{{Quote|Look at this. Ever since the XP-38 came out, they just aren't in demand.''"<br />"''It'll be enough.|Luke Skywalker laments the low selling price of his landspeeder to Obi-Wan Kenobi|<ref name="Episode IV">{{Film|IV}}</ref>}}
[[File:V35_Rebels.jpg|thumb|right|270px|A V-35 Courier landspeeder]]
A '''landspeeder''', also known as a '''hovercar''',<ref name="Seeds of Starlight">''[[The High Republic: Seeds of Starlight]]''</ref> was a ground transportation vehicle capable of hovering slightly that enabled transit at relatively high speeds. [[Luke Skywalker]] owned an [[X-34 landspeeder]], which he and his newfound friend [[C-3PO]] used to travel to the [[Jundland Wastes]] to seek out [[R2-D2]] when he escaped from the [[Lars homestead|Lars moisture farm]]. Later, he used the landspeeder to [[pilot]] himself, [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], and the [[droid]]s C-3PO and R2-D2 from the Jundland Wastes to [[Mos Eisley]] following the destruction of the Lars homestead. After the group arrived at Mos Eisley and chartered [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]] to fly them to [[Alderaan]] on the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', Luke sold his landspeeder for 2,000 [[Galactic Credit Standard|credits]] to help cover their fare. Luke lamented the price he was given, noting that ever since the new model of landspeeder had come out, the old one just didn't sell like it used to.<ref name="Episode IV" />

Types of landspeeders include the [[RGC-18 landspeeder]], the [[V-35 Courier]],<ref name="head">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Head to Head]]''</ref> the [[T-44 landspeeder]],<ref name="tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> and the [[XP-38 sport speeder]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> and the [[V-40]].<ref name="Smuggler's Run">''[[Smuggler's Run: A Han Solo & Chewbacca Adventure]]''</ref>

